{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest knowledge of Japan's delight\nA land of cherry blossoms and rising sun's first light\n\nDay one thou shalt arrive in Tokyo's bustling streets\nWhere ancient temples meet modern city's frantic beats\nVisit Senso-ji's famous Nakamise shopping street\nWhere merchants peddle wares and travelers seek a treat\n\nNext morning rise early to witness the sun's ascent\nAt Tokyo Skytree's observation deck thou shalt be bent\nOn gazing out upon the city's sprawling might\nAnd taking in the vistas of a Tokyo morning bright\n\nDay two thou shalt venture to the Meiji Shrine's hallowed grounds\nA tranquil oasis in the midst of Tokyo's din and crowds\nWalk through the forested paths and pay homage to the past\nAnd breathe in the serenity that this sacred place doth cast\n\nDay three thou shalt depart for Kyoto the imperial city\nWhere geishas once danced and nobles held court with dignity\nVisit the Fushimi Inari shrine where thousands of vermillion gates\nDo stand like sentinels guarding the entrance to the sacred state\n\nNext morning rise early to watch the sun rise over the hills\nAt Kinkaku-ji's temple of gold thou shalt behold its golden thrills\nA sight most wondrous and a treasure to behold in Japan\nA testament to the land's rich history and mystic plan\n\nDay four thou shalt visit Arashiyama's bamboo forest deep\nWhere towering stalks do sway and whisper secrets in the breeze\nWalk along the riverbanks and take in the scenic views\nAnd marvel at the beauty of this enchanted land anew\n\nDay five thou shalt depart for Osaka the city of delight\nWhere food and drink do flow like rivers in the night\nVisit the Osaka Castle's keep and learn of its storied past\nAnd sample the local cuisine that doth delight the senses at last\n\nDay six thou shalt return to Tokyo the city of lights\nWhere neon billboards shine and the city's energy doth